<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Pohoří na Šumavě–Kamenec circuit — Pohoří na Šumavě–Kamenec circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start at the parking place at the end of Pohoří na Šumavě, walk back through the village past the church and follow green across the meadows, past the giant cedar and former Schwarzviertel, to Kamenec and Pod Kamencem. Follow the fence to the first gate. Continue along the unmarked Austrian forest road through its southern bend and eastward, take the left fork towards Karlstift through the second gate, then turn right at the following junction towards the boundary stones. Follow the blue 105 border course past the 1661 three-country pillar and Antoniusquelle to Pohoří CZ/A, then green back to the same parking place.

Use this walk in snow-free daylight in spring, summer or autumn. Marking is partial and the Austrian forest-road section is unmarked: carry a map and compass. Stay on the existing admitted forest roads and marked walking course through protected grounds; respect wetland margins, trees, nesting birds and current forestry or conservation signs. Rough and wet footing can be difficult. Passage through the two gates is not guaranteed. If a required gate or route section is closed or passage is prohibited, this exact itinerary is unavailable; no equivalent detour is supplied.

The complete course is approximately 11.6 km, calculated from the captured OpenStreetMap path; allow about 240 minutes with inherited approximate 271 m ascent and 271 m descent estimates, which are not surveyed elevation figures. Geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0, from the complete actual captured API XML. This is a descriptive planning route, not navigation-grade, and contains no elevation data.

